  "id": "centering",
  "term": "centering",
  "definition": "Centering, in this context, is the nervous system’s early, usually unconscious adjustment of pitch during speech so that an utterance shifts toward an intended target or typical pitch over time. It reflects fine, online stabilization of vocal output and may not depend entirely on auditory feedback.",
